WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.800
What if just one
lifestyle change

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.600
could help you
avoid getting cancer,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.440
or diabetes,
or heart disease,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.880
or high blood pressure?

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.160
This one change could cut
your risk of chronic disease

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.000
and add years to your life.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.760
Well, the simple solution to
so many of these problems

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.080
is to eat a healthy diet.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.520
In other words, one centered
around whole plant foods.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.840
I'm your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.920
There is a lot of demand for
information about fasting.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.360
And as luck would have it,

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.240
more and more research
is released every day.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:44.080
Today we look at the practice of
fasting to reverse type 2 diabetes.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.440
Currently, nearly half a billion
adults have diabetes,

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.440
and a 50% increase is
expected in another generation.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.120
I've got tons of videos on
the best diets for diabetes,

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.680
but what about no diet at all?
More than a century ago,

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.720
fasting was said to bring
about the cure of diabetes,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.160
speedily arresting its development
and causing complete disappearance

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.040
of all its manifestations
in several days or weeks.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.480
Even so, starvation is
guaranteed to lead to

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.440
the complete disappearance
of you, if kept up long enough.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.280
What's the point of fasting it away,
if it's just going to come raging back

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.000
as soon as you restart the diet
that caused it in the first place?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.360
Might it be useful to kind of
kickstart a healthier diet?

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.840
Let's see what the science says.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.240
Type 2 diabetes has long been
recognized as a disease of excess,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.320
a disease of the idle rich,

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.880
by which they mean anyone
who doesn't practice

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.360
sustained vigorous
bodily exertion every day,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.320
and earning enough to regularly
eat more than they need.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:51.360
So diabetes is preventable,
but then maybe it's also treatable.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:59.040
If we are dying of overeating, maybe
we can be saved by undereating.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:04.320
Remarkably this was suggested about
2,000 years ago in an Ayurvedic text.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.640
Diabetics were encouraged
to live like a saint, walk for, oh,

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:16.160
800 or 900 miles, dig a pond, or live
only on cow dung and cow urine.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.720
That reminds me of the Rollo diet
for diabetes proposed in 1797,

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.400
composed of a diet of rancid meat.
That was on top of the ipecac-like drugs

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.520
he used to produce
severe sickness and vomiting.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.520
Anything that produces sickness has
a temporary effect in relieving diabetes

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.560
by diminishing the
quantity of food eaten.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.400
And his diet plan —
congealed blood for lunch

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.400
and spoiled meat for dinner —
certainly had that effect.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.640
Similar benefits were seen in
diabetics during the siege of Paris

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:55.600
in the Franco-Prussian War,
leading to the advice to

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.760
'mangez le moins possible'
(eat as little as possible).

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.520
That was formalized into
the Allen Starvation treatment,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.640
considered to be the greatest medical
advance in the treatment of diabetes

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:14.960
prior to the discovery of insulin.
Before insulin, there was the Allen Era.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.200
He noted reports in the clinical literature
of even severe diabetics clearing up

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:27.200
on wasting diseases like tuberculosis,
so he decided to put it to the test.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.400
He found that even the
most severe type of diabetes,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.840
he could clear sugar from
people's urine within 10 days.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.000
Of course, that's the easy part.
It's maintaining it

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.320
once you start eating again,
for which he stuck to two principles:

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.840
keeping them underweight
and restricting the quantity of fat.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.240
A severe diabetic can be
symptom-free for days or weeks,

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.760
but add some butter or olive oil and
the disease can come raging back.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:01.200
As I covered before, diabetes
is a disease of fat toxicity.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.920
Infuse fat into people's
veins through an IV,

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.040
and by using a high-tech
type of MRI scanner,

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.120
you can show in real time the buildup
of fat in muscle cells within hours,

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.080
accompanied by an increase
in insulin resistance.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.000
The same thing happens when you put
people on a high-fat diet for three days,

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:20.400
or even just one day,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.840
or even just a single meal can increase
insulin resistance within six hours.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.200
Acute dietary fat intake rapidly
increases insulin resistance.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.400
Why do we care?
Because insulin resistance

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.760
in our muscles, in the context
of too many calories, leads to

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:43.920
the buildup of liver fat, which leads
to the buildup of fat in the pancreas,

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.200
which is eventually what
causes diabetes.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.160
Type 2 diabetes can now
be understood as a state

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.000
of excess fat in the
liver and pancreas

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.080
and remains reversible for at least
10 years in most individuals.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.000
Put people on a very low-calorie
diet, 700 calories a day,

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.480
and fat can get sucked
out of your muscle cells,

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.200
and you get a corresponding
boost in insulin sensitivity.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.880
Fat is then sucked out of your liver,

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:10.160
and if you keep it up the fat gets
sucked out of your pancreas.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.920
And if you catch it early enough
that can mean a reversal

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:18.640
of your type 2 diabetes, meaning
normal sugars on a normal diet.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.160
With the loss of 15% of body weight,
nearly 90% of those who've had

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.040
type 2 diabetes for less than four
years can achieve remission,

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.760
where it may only be reversible in 50%
of those who've lived with the disease

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.760
for longer than eight years.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:38.640
That's better than bariatric surgery,
where those losing even more weight

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:42.160
only got 62 and 26% remissions.

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:46.240
Your forks are better
than the surgeon's knives.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.120
Here's how much weight you have to
lose to achieve various remission rates

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.920
for those who've had diabetes
for an average of three years.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:58.560
Lose about 30 pounds and most
newly diagnosed type 2 diabetics

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.920
can reverse their disease. So an
extended bout of physician-supervised,

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.880
water-only fasting could get you there,

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.240
but you have to maintain
the weight loss.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.720
One of the things we
can say with certainty

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.280
is that if you regain the weight,
you regain your diabetes.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.080
To bring it full circle,
the initial euphoria about

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.320
medicine's greatest miracle,
the discovery of insulin in 1921,

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:29.360
soon gave way to the realization
that while it was literally a life-saver

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:33.760
for type 1 diabetics, the use of insulin
on its own in type 2 diabetics

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.880
would not be enough to prevent
the later onset of complications

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:40.480
like kidney failure, blindness,
stroke, amputations.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:46.960
So, as argued by one the most famous
diabetes pioneers, Elliot Joslin,

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:52.080
self-discipline on diet and exercise,
as it was in the days prior to insulin,

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:55.360
should be central to the
management of diabetes.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.360
Did you know that
caloric restriction

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:02.800
can boost levels of brain-
derived neurotrophic factor,

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.088
otherwise known as BDNF?

00:07:05.088 --> 00:07:08.311
In fact, I just wrote
a chapter on it

00:07:08.311 --> 00:07:10.827
in my upcoming book,
"How Not to Age".

00:07:10.827 --> 00:07:13.156
Anyway, here's the story.

00:07:13.825 --> 00:07:16.560
For over a century, fasting has
been espoused as a treatment

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.920
of supposed “great utility in
the preservation of health,”

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:24.160
especially rejuvenating the body,
but above all the mind.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:29.120
But fast people even just 18 hours,
and they get all hungry and irritable.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.640
After one or two days positive mood
goes down, negative mood goes up,

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.320
and by 72 hours people
can feel sad, self-blaming,

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.000
and suffer a loss in libido.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.160
But then something
strange starts to happen.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.720
After a few days, people experience
a “fasting-induced mood enhancement…

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.240
decreased anxiety, depression,
fatigue, and improved vigor.”

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:55.680
And that’s what studies tend
to show across the board.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.320
Once you get over the hump,
fasters frequently experience

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.120
“an increased level of vigilance and…
mood improvement,

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:06.000
a subjective feeling of well-being,
and sometimes [even] euphoria.”

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.200
And no wonder, as by
then your endorphin levels

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.080
may shoot up nearly 50 percent.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.720
This enhancement of mood,
alertness, and calm

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.200
makes a certain amount
of evolutionary sense.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:21.040
Yeah, your body wants you
to feel crappy initially

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.160
so you continue eating day
to day when food is available,

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:27.920
but if you go a couple days
without food your body realizes

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.040
it can’t have you moping back
in the cave—you’ve got to

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:34.400
get motivated to get out
there and find some calories.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:39.840
So, can fasting be used for
mood disorders like depression?

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.240
Yeah, it’s great that you
can get people to feel better

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:44.800
after a few days of fasting,
but the critical question

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.560
revolves around “the persistence
of mood improvement over time”

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.000
once you start eating again.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:55.440
You don’t know until...
you put it to the test.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.960
Interestingly, the little published
evidence we have comes out of

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:04.397
Japan and the former Soviet Union,
and some of it is just ridiculous.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.320
Ten days of fasting, but they
also kept them in bed all day

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.200
completely isolated, with no
contact with the outside world.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.680
So, if people got better or
worse it would be impossible

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.080
to tease out the effects of
just the fasting component.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.600
But they did apparently get
better with efficacy supposedly

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:24.080
demonstrated in 31 out of 36
patients suffering from depression.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.800
They conclude that fasting
therapy may provide an alternative

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.440
to the use of antidepressant drugs,

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.400
considering it “a kind of shock therapy.”

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.880
People are so relieved
to just be eating again,

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.560
to get out of solitary confinement,

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:40.480
to even just get out of bed
they report feeling better.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.600
Yeah, but that was at
the time of discharge.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.960
How did they feel the next day,
the next week, the next month?

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:52.000
Fasting is by definition unsustainable,
so ideally what we want to see

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.320
are some kind of longer-lasting effects.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.320
So, what the researchers did was
follow-up with a few hundred patients,

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.680
not just a few months later
but a few years later.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.080
Of the 69 who were evidently
suffering from depression,

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.480
90 percent reported feeling
good or excellent results

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:10.800
at the end of the 10-day
fast and remarkably, years later

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:14.560
87 percent of the 62 that replied
claimed that they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.080
still doing good.
&nbsp;

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:18.320
Now there was no control
group, so we don’t know

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.360
if they would have done just
as well or better without the fast,

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:25.360
and it was just self-reports,
so maybe there was response bias

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:29.520
where you try to please the researchers,
or maybe they were afraid

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.760
otherwise they’d get
sent back to the hole.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.080
We have no idea, but we
do have good evidence

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:38.000
for the short-term mood benefits.
The question is why.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.720
In addition to the endorphins when
you fast and the surge in serotonin,

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:46.560
the so-called happiness hormone,
there is a bump in BDNF,

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:48.560
brain-derived neurotrophic factor,

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:51.760
considered to play a crucial
role in mood disorders.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.760
And it’s not just because
you perk up rodents with it.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.400
Humans with major
depression have lower levels

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.920
circulating in their blood stream.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:04.000
Autopsy studies of suicide victims
show only about half the BDNF

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.640
in certain key brain
regions compared to controls,

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.840
suggesting it may play an
important role in suicidal behavior.

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.720
You can boost BDNF with
antidepressant drugs

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:17.360
and electroshock, or with calorie
restriction—a 70 percent boost

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.280
in levels after three months cutting 25
percent of calories out of their daily diet.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.880
What effect does fasting
and a plant-based diet

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.840
have on traumatic brain
injury and migraines?

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:29.680
Let’s find out.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:34.800
An uncontrolled and unpublished study
purported to show a beneficial effect

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.640
of fasting on migraine headaches,
but fasting may be more likely

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:42.960
to trigger a migraine than help it.
In fact, skipped meals

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.120
are among one of the most
consistently identified

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.520
dietary triggers
of headaches in general.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:52.480
In a review of hundreds of fasts at the
TrueNorth Health Center in California,

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:57.280
the incidence of headache was nearly
one in three, but TrueNorth also

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:02.160
published a remarkable case
report on post-traumatic headache.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.080
The CDC estimates that more
than a million Americans sustain

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:09.520
traumatic brain injuries every
year, and chronic pain

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:13.520
is a common complication,
as in like three-quarters

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.040
suffering such an injury.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:19.280
There are drugs, of course, to treat it.
There are always drugs.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.560
And if that doesn't work, surgery:
cutting the nerves to your head

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:26.880
to stop the pain. Well, what
about fasting and plants?

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.600
A highly debilitating condition,
difficult to manage,

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:33.040
a 52-year-old woman
presents with unremitting,

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.040
chronic post-traumatic headache.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:41.280
And when I say chronic, I mean
chronic---pain for 16 years---

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.800
but who then achieved
long-term relief following fasting,

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.760
followed by an exclusively plant-based
diet, free of added sugar, oil, or salt.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:54.320
Before then she had tried drug
after drug, after drug, after drug,

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:59.200
after drug with no relief, suffering
in constant pain her entire life.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.800
Started out in constant pain,
but then after the fast,

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.920
the intensity of her pain was cut in
half, and though she was still having

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:10.160
daily headaches, at least there
were some pain-free periods.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.960
Six months later she tried it again,
and eventually her headaches

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.760
were mild, under 10 minutes,
and infrequent,

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:19.840
and she continued that way
months and even years later.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.800
Now, of course, it's hard
to disentangle the effects

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.920
of the fasting from the effects of
the whole food plant-based diet

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.320
she remained on
those ensuing years.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:33.680
You've heard of analgesics---painkillers.
Well, there are some foods that may be

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:39.120
pro-algesic: pain promoting, such
as foods high in arachidonic acid,

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.600
which includes include
meats, dairy, and eggs.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:46.000
So the lowering of arachidonic acid,
from which our body makes a range

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:49.280
of pro-inflammatory compounds,
may be accomplished by eating

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:52.160
a more plant-based diet.
So maybe that contributed

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.640
to the benefit in
the fasting case.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:58.640
Whereas many plant foods are high
in anti-inflammatory components.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:02.400
So in terms of migraine headaches,
more plant foods and less animal foods

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:06.880
may help, but you don't know
until you put it to the test.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.960
The researchers figured a plant-based
diet may offer the best of both worlds,

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.080
so they designed a randomized,
controlled crossover study

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.560
where those with recurrent
migraines were randomized

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:20.720
to eat a strictly plant-based
diet or to take a placebo pill.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.560
And then the groups switched.
During the placebo phase

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:27.840
half said the pain got better,
half said the pain remained the same

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:32.880
or got worse, but during the dietary
portion they almost all got better.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.360
During that first block, the diet group
experienced significant improvements

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.040
in headache number, pain intensity,

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:41.360
days with headaches, and a
reduction in the amount

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:46.320
of painkillers they needed to take.
In fact, it worked a little too good.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.280
Many individuals were
unwilling to complete the study

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.120
by returning to their previous diets.
Remember, they were supposed to

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.000
go back to their regular diets
and take a pill instead,

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.080
but they felt so much better that
they were like, "No way, José."

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:03.280
And we've seen this with other trials,
where those trying plant-based diets

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:08.000
felt so good, they often refused to
abandon them, screwing up the study.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:12.240
So plant-based diets can
sometimes work a little too well.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:16.320
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:19.520
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:23.280
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:27.600
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:32.720
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:36.000
please go to the Nutrition Facts Podcast
landing page.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.400
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:42.640
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite to each of these topics.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:47.600
My latest two books are
“How to Survive a Pandemic”,

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:51.360
available on e-book, audiobook,
or actual book.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:55.440
And the “How Not to Diet Cookbook”,
with more than 100 recipes for

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:57.600
delicious and nutritious meals.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:02.960
All the proceeds I receive from
the sales of my books go to charity.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:07.600
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.440
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:13.600
on the latest in nutrition research
via bite-sized videos and articles.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.440
Everything on the website is free.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.560
There’s no ads, no corporate sponsorship.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:22.080
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:25.360
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:28.320
as a tribute to my grandmother,

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:34.720
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

